ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution}: From the given problem, we have
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
y=-x+3 \\
y=\frac{2}{x}
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Therefore, $-x+3=\frac{2}{x}$, solving this gives $x_1=1$, $x_2=2$, $y_1=2$, $y_2=1$,
therefore, the points are \boxed{A(1, 2)}, \boxed{B(2, 1)}.

